{"data": [{"id": "2122132201101766916", "author_id": "30989189", "text": "@omarsar0 Boring is super hard", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:58:38.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/fepavani/status/2122132201101766916", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122131904447303811", "author_id": "2114906570303905792", "text": "@nakularora @omarsar0 A flaky API response is a good test case: keep the raw input and expected output, then rerun it after each prompt or tool change.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:57:27.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/BudgtStore/status/2122131904447303811", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122131706803286201", "author_id": "2114906570303905792", "text": "@jamesj_cottrell @omarsar0 A deterministic harness turns an impressive demo into something you can actually debug and trust.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:56:40.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/BudgtStore/status/2122131706803286201", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122126845206217170", "author_id": "1894319334874329088", "text": "@omarsar0 95% per step sounds fine until you chain 20 of them. that's 36% end to end", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:37:21.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/choroukmalmoum/status/2122126845206217170", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122126823480086665", "author_id": "38472599", "text": "@omarsar0 Do you have an example here that you could share?", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:37:16.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/nakularora/status/2122126823480086665", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122126293420650724", "author_id": "2042409707755741184", "text": "@omarsar0 That's why Puppetmaster/Marionette continue to thrive :)", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:35:10.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/CaryPalmerr/status/2122126293420650724", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122124504684196279", "author_id": "2104726095010332672", "text": "@omarsar0 Every agentic demo is twelve agents talking to each other. Every production system is a pile of if statements with an LLM on call. The boring parts are the product.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:28:03.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/ScoutedAI/status/2122124504684196279", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122121659226481146", "author_id": "2104770760921272320", "text": "@omarsar0 The unsexy part is exactly where most demos fall apart — everyone shows the agent doing the clever bit, nobody shows the verifier catching it hallucinating a filename. Boring deterministic steps are the whole product, the LLM is just the flexible glue in between.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:16:45.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/YunaElira/status/2122121659226481146", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122118324163326140", "author_id": "45745017", "text": "@omarsar0 ➕", "lang": "qme", "created_at": "2026-11-16T00:03:30.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/virenbaraiya/status/2122118324163326140", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122115455167218025", "author_id": "1736486334972473344", "text": "@omarsar0 Our agents should be as “lazy” as us and want to be involved in mundane things as often as us. \n\nThey should build/own/evolve the deterministic systems.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:52:06.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/rickwong888/status/2122115455167218025", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122114889225544099", "author_id": "1446309913152552960", "text": "@omarsar0 This is why evals matter so much. Without verifiers and proper quality gates, adding more agents can just make failures harder to catch and debug.", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:49:51.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/himlabs/status/2122114889225544099", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122114355940536440", "author_id": "2110357929371316224", "text": "@omarsar0 A plain schema check between steps catches a lot: bad output fails loudly instead of the next agent improvising around it 💡 Do you run evaluators after every step or only at the end?", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:47:44.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/botmancer/status/2122114355940536440", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122109381580034537", "author_id": "1842901", "text": "@DrDonPerugini @omarsar0 ❤️", "lang": "qme", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:27:58.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/mckeague/status/2122109381580034537", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122107587495612731", "author_id": "818802423007350784", "text": "@omarsar0 So the real trick is knowing which parts to hard-code and which parts to leave to the model — where do you draw that line in practice?", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:20:50.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/will58798103/status/2122107587495612731", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}, {"id": "2122107261246201916", "author_id": "1922959509456068608", "text": "@omarsar0 this is it. ive seen people spin up ten bots talking to each other when a basic automation would do. every extra step is another place it can fall over", "lang": "en", "created_at": "2026-11-15T23:19:32.000Z", "url": "https://x.com/seancroweai/status/2122107261246201916", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "30989189", "username": "fepavani", "name": "Fernando Pavani", "verified": false}, {"id": "3448284313", "username": "omarsar0", "name": "elvis", "verified": false}, {"id": "2114906570303905792", "username": "BudgtStore", "name": "BudgtStore", "verified": false}, {"id": "38472599", "username": "nakularora", "name": "Nakul Arora", "verified": false}, {"id": "1233864069377077250", "username": "jamesj_cottrell", "name": "James Cottrell", "verified": false}, {"id": "1894319334874329088", "username": "choroukmalmoum", "name": "Chorouk Malmoum", "verified": false}, {"id": "2042409707755741184", "username": "CaryPalmerr", "name": "Palmer", "verified": false}, {"id": "2104726095010332672", "username": "ScoutedAI", "name": "Alex Carter", "verified": false}, {"id": "2104770760921272320", "username": "YunaElira", "name": "Yuna Han", "verified": false}, {"id": "45745017", "username": "virenbaraiya", "name": "Viren", "verified": false}, {"id": "1736486334972473344", "username": "rickwong888", "name": "Rick Wong", "verified": false}, {"id": "1446309913152552960", "username": "himlabs", "name": "Himanshu Singh", "verified": false}, {"id": "2110357929371316224", "username": "botmancer", "name": "William Gibson", "verified": false}, {"id": "1842901", "username": "mckeague", "name": "David McKeague", "verified": false}, {"id": "917853275788996608", "username": "DrDonPerugini", "name": "Dr Don Perugini", "verified": false}, {"id": "818802423007350784", "username": "will58798103", "name": "everett", "verified": false}, {"id": "1922959509456068608", "username": "seancroweai", "name": "Sean Crowe", "verified": false}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2122132201101766916", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzow6b5zflp3mq8smalktg1lism7x", "oldest_id": "2122107261246201916", "result_count": 15}}